From: perf session 2026-09-12
Subject: [PATCH 0039] pmb887x display path: per-word costs of the DIF/DMAC/VIC chain

A redrawing J2ME app (the built-in stopwatch, ~57 framebuffer updates/s)
pushes every LCD word through DIF TX FIFO -> DMAC request -> VIC, and
that chain was 44 % of the vCPU on the wasm64 build (the guest never
halts in that state, so its clock runs at guest-MIPS/125 - the user's
"Java timers at 0.1x").  Per word/burst the models did:

  - vic_update_state: scanned all 170 lines (twice: irq + fiq) on every
    level change, including changes to the same level - 10 % of the vCPU.
    Now an asserted-line bitmap is walked, and an unchanged level is a
    no-op (the pending state cannot have changed).
  - dif_update_gpio_state re-drove CS1..3/CD/RD/WR through the GPIO
    block (and on to the LCD/SSI handlers, each a QOM cast) for every
    FIFO word; dif_trigger_dma re-drove all eight DMAC request lines per
    event - qemu_set_irq 10 %.  Every consumer (GPIO proxy, lcd_handle_cd/
    rd/wr, ssi_cs_default, dmac_handle_signal) is level-idempotent, so an
    unchanged level is skipped (caches reset to "unknown" on device reset).
  - dif_mux ran a 32-iteration bit loop per word: now four byte-lane
    table lookups (rebuilt in dif_update_mux; bit-for-bit the same value).
  - dmac_transfer_memory read a memory source one word per
    address_space_read; a memory->peripheral burst with an incrementing
    source now reads the burst once (the FIFO still sees each word).
  - pmb887x_srb_set_isr tested all 32 bits; it walks the set bits.

Measured (tools/stopwatch.mjs, virtual s per wall s while the stopwatch
runs): 0.19 -> 0.33 (25 -> 41 MIPS) for the VIC + pin/request caches; the
mux tables / burst read / set_isr are inside the run-to-run noise on top
(0.32 +- 0.02).  Boot (idlebench --quick, both orders, with 0040):
t0.5G -2..-3 %, t1.3G -1..-3 %.  Gates: op-suite 1156/1156 identical,
native suite 4/4, dist-jit bootcheck s75/el71/ke800, lockstep 250e6.
The wasm64 build additionally sets -Dqom_cast_debug=false
(scripts/build-qemu-wasm64.sh): -3..-5 % on every boot milestone.

